  {
   "id": "s02",
   "narration": "The retry signature takes a count and a delay. Inside, the loop calls the function. When it fails, the backoff waits longer each time. Once the attempts run out, we look at the loop again.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "code",
    "heading": "A retry decorator",
    "language": "python",
    "code": "import time\nimport random\n\n\ndef retry(times, delay=0.5):\n    \"\"\"Retry a function when it raises.\"\"\"\n\n    def decorator(fn):\n        def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n            last = None\n            for attempt in range(times):\n                try:\n                    return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n                except Exception as err:\n                    last = err\n                    wait = delay * 2 ** attempt\n                    wait += random.random() * 0.1\n                    time.sleep(wait)\n            raise last\n\n        return wrapper\n\n    return decorator\n\n\n@retry(times=3)\ndef fetch(url):\n    return download(url)",
    "highlights": [
     {
      "lines": "5",
      "label": "Signature"
     },
